    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "You can now add projects for clients: there's a new **Projects** page where you pick the client when adding a project, and the list shows each project with the client's name. Both Playwright tests pass when run with `bin/e2e`.\n\n**The server is Spring Boot, not OfficeFloor.** The request asked for an OfficeFloor server, but the codebase and `CLAUDE.md` are Spring, so I built it the Spring way, matching the existing client feature.\n\n- **Database:** a new migration, `V3__create_project.sql`, adds a `project` table. Each project must point to an existing client.\n- **Server:** a new `project` package with endpoints to list projects (`GET /api/projects`) and add one (`POST /api/projects`). Each project comes back with its client's id and name, loaded in one query. Adding a project with a missing name or an unknown client is rejected with a 400 error.\n- **Test setup:** I changed the test-only controller so it can seed projects. Resetting now clears the project table before the client table. The database won't normally empty a table another table refers to, so reset turns that check off for the moment it runs.\n- **Front end:** the new Projects page sits in the nav after Clients and follows the same layout and error handling as the Clients page. The client dropdown starts on \"Select a client\", and the form shows an error if you submit without choosing one. Every element the test looks for has the `data-testid` it expects.\n\nThere's no audit record when a project is created, because the test doesn't expect one.",
